      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: add Herdr plugin",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- add a Herdr plugin manifest with boxes, warmup, prewarm, connect, repository job, and doctor actions\n- add a hidden Crabbox adapter that safely consumes Herdr invocation context without requiring jq, Python, or Node at runtime\n- add build/path pinning, documentation, packaging tests, and CLI unit tests\n\n## Why\n\nHerdr can install executable workflow plugins directly from GitHub subdirectories. This gives Crabbox users native Herdr actions and managed panes while keeping provider credentials, lease ownership, repository sync, and job behavior inside the Crabbox CLI.\n\n## User impact\n\nAfter release, users can install the integration with:\n\n```sh\nherdr plugin install openclaw/crabbox/plugins/herdr\n```\n\nThe plugin does not install keybindings or lifecycle hooks. Normal Crabbox job stop policies still apply.\n\n## Publication\n\nNo Herdr repository PR is required. Herdr installs manifests from GitHub repository subdirectories, and its marketplace automatically indexes public repositories carrying the `herdr-plugin` topic. After this change and a compatible Crabbox release land on `main`, add that topic to `openclaw/crabbox` so the marketplace advertises a working default-branch install.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `go test ./...`\n- `go vet ./...`\n- `go test -race ./internal/cli -run 'TestHerdrPlugin|TestNonBlankLines' -count=1`\n- `node --test scripts/herdr-plugin.test.js`\n- `scripts/check-docs.sh`\n- Herdr 0.7.3 end-to-end smoke: link manifest, create repository workspace, invoke boxes action, verify managed pane changes into the repository cwd, focus pane, and close pane\n",
        "branch": "codex/add-herdr-plugin",
